# design-taste-astro (translated from design-taste-frontend)

Translated anti-slop rules for the **ngemper.ai** Astro + vanilla CSS stack.
Skip the React / Tailwind / Motion / GSAP sections of the upstream skill; keep
everything that survives without those tools.

## Brief inference

Before any page-level work, state a one-line **Design Read**:

> Reading this as: `<page kind>` for `<audience>`, with a `<vibe>` language,
> leaning toward `<aesthetic family>`.

ngemper.ai reads as: **single-page POC planner for Indonesian budget travelers
on a first SEA overland trip, with a field-guide / editorial language, leaning
toward cool-ink + mustard on off-white, calm motion, no Awwwards tricks.**

## Three dials (set per task, baseline `8 / 6 / 4`)

- `DESIGN_VARIANCE` (1-10) - layout asymmetry / off-grid compositions
- `MOTION_INTENSITY` (1-10) - hover, entry, scroll-driven movement
- `VISUAL_DENSITY` (1-10) - section padding, card density

Translate to vanilla-CSS:

- `MOTION` > 3 must respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Use CSS
  `transition` + `@keyframes` + `IntersectionObserver` for scroll reveals.
  No `window.addEventListener('scroll')` listener loops.
- Animate only `transform` and `opacity`.
- `DESIGN_VARIANCE` 4-10 must declare explicit mobile collapse
  (`< 768px` -> single column, `max-w-[var(--max)] mx-auto`).

## Hard rules

- **Zero em-dashes (`—`)** anywhere visible. Use `-`, `.`, `,`, or `:`. If a
  string contains `—`, rewrite before shipping.
- **Hero fits the viewport**: headline ≤ 2 lines, subtext ≤ 20 words and
  ≤ 4 lines, primary CTA visible without scroll.
- **Hero top padding**: max `6rem` at desktop. Use `min-height: 100dvh`, never
  `100vh` (iOS Safari address-bar jump).
- **One eyebrow per 3 sections, max**. Hero counts as 1. Mechanical check:
  `text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing` on small labels above headlines
  must total `ceil(sectionCount / 3)` or fewer.
- **One theme per page** (light or dark, locked).
- **One accent color** across the whole page - lock it in `:root`, audit every
  CTA / link / border-active state before shipping.
- **One shape system** (corner-radius scale). Mixed allowed only with a
  documented rule (e.g. "buttons pill, cards 4px, inputs 4px") followed
  everywhere.
- **CTA contrast**: every CTA label must pass WCAG AA against its background
  (4.5:1 body, 3:1 large text 18px+). Audit before shipping.
- **No duplicate CTA intent** on one page (e.g. don't ship "Copy share URL"
  next to a "Share" link that opens the same thing).
- **Real assets or labeled placeholders**. No div-based fake product UI.
  No fake version labels in hero (`V0.6`, `BETA`, `INVITE-ONLY`).

## AI tells to avoid

- Fraunces, Instrument Serif, or any LLM-favorite display serif as default.
  Default to a strong sans display (Bricolage Grotesque, Cabinet Grotesk,
  Geist, Sora).
- Inter as the default sans body unless the brand explicitly asks for it.
  Source Sans 3 is acceptable here as an Indonesian-readable body face.
- AI-purple / neon glow / centered dark-mesh hero as default.
- Warm beige + brass + oxblood + espresso cream palette for premium-consumer
  briefs. ngemper.ai uses **cool ink** + **mustard** + **forest** instead -
  not the warm-paper cream family.
- Three equal feature cards. Use asymmetric grids or stacked layouts.
- Generic `border-t` + `border-b` on every row of long lists. Use hairlines
  sparingly or group with cards.
- Em-dash anywhere (see above).
- Decorative colored status dots before every nav/badge/list item.
- Section-numbering eyebrows (`01 / INDEX`, `006 · Capabilities`).
- Locale / city / time / weather strips unless the brief is genuinely
  place-focused.
- Scroll cues (`Scroll`, `↓ scroll`) and animated mouse-wheel icons.
- Photo-credit captions as decoration (`Field study no. 12 · Ines Caetano`).
- "Quietly in use at" / "Quietly trusted by" social-proof headers.
- Mock-humble industry references ("We respect the French ones") in copy.

## Performance & a11y

- LCP < 2.5s. Hero image (`/hero-overland.png`) must be preloaded.
- INP < 200ms. Heavy work off main thread (no scroll listeners in render).
- CLS < 0.1. Reserve aspect-ratio on iframes, images, map embeds.
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` must collapse all infinite loops, parallax,
  and entry transitions.
- Form / select / button labels must pass WCAG AA contrast.

## Stack constraints (from project.mdc - always primary)

- Astro 5 static, TypeScript strict, vanilla CSS, vanilla TS island, Vitest.
- No React, Tailwind, Motion, GSAP, map SDKs.
- Money: IDR only, badges `estimate` / `approx` / `flight avg`.
- Maps: Google Maps Embed iframe only. Placeholder if key missing.
- Domain logic in `src/lib/*`, TDD with Vitest before UI for totals / rank /
  compose.
- Footer: `Estimates · curated Aug 2026 · not for booking`.

These two rule files (`project.mdc` + `design-taste-astro.mdc`) are the only
overlays. Do not invent new wrappers or conventions.
